Align the stack of every thread mln-rs starts on riscv64 musl.

musl's riscv64 __clone doesn't align the stack it's given, and
pthread_create aligns a new thread's stack top to 8 bytes only, below the
thread's TLS. A thread can start 8 bytes off the 16 that the RISC-V psABI
requires, depending on the TLS size of the libraries loaded so far, and its
calls into host callbacks are misaligned too. The JVM's riscv64 upcall stub
then reads its frame data 8 bytes off and crashes, which killed the
Kotlin/JVM suite on linux-musl-riscv64. louwers/mln-rs#357 upstreams this.

